==English==
[[File:Astigmatism (Eye).png|thumb|]]

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|a-|pos1=negative prefix}} + stem of {{der|en|grc|στίγμα||mark, point}} + {{affix|en|-ism}}. {{coin|en|William Whewell|in=1846|nat=English|occ=polymath}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈstɪɡmətɪzm̩/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-astigmatism.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|optics}} A defect of a [[lens]] such that light rays coming from a point do not meet at a [[focal point]] so that the image is blurred.
# {{lb|en|pathology}} A disorder of the vision, usually due to a misshapen [[cornea]], such that light does not focus correctly on the [[retina]] causing a blurred image.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|astigmia}}

